. The Americans had been stung in the 100 metres by the disqualification of " [:a {:href "/athletes/78523"} "Eddie Hart"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78966"} "Rey Robinson"] " when they showed up late for their quarter-final heats, having used an incorrect schedule to determine when they were to run next. Robinson was not chosen for the relay as 200 silver medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/78117"} "Larry Black"] " was picked for his turn-running ability. In the final, he opened up and there was little to choose between him and Kornelyuk at the first exchange. " [:a {:href "/athletes/79114"} "Robert Taylor"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79130"} "Gerald Tinker"] " then gave the US a big lead by the time the baton got to Hart for the anchor leg. Borzov was four metres down and possibly gained a little on Hart but the US won easily with a world record time of 38.19."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "38.96 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "38.54 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "38.19 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/78117"} "Larry Black"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/79114"} "Robert Taylor"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/79130"} "Gerald Tinker"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78523"} "Eddie Hart"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78181"} "Larry Burton"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78966"} "Rey Robinson"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {:class